To solve the problem of finding the maximum subarray sum with the earliest start and end indices, we use a modified version of **Kadane's algorithm**. The algorithm keeps track of the current subarray sum and its starting index. At each step, if adding the current element to the existing subarray sum is better than starting a new subarray, we extend the current subarray. Otherwise, we start a new subarray. Alongside, we maintain the best sum found so far and update the indices whenever we find a new maximum or an equivalent sum with an earlier start or end.

The solution ensures that among all subarrays with the same maximum sum, the one with the earliest start (and earliest end if necessary) is chosen. This is handled by comparing the current subarray's start index with the best start index and updating accordingly.

